  "grammar_explanations": [
    {
      "slug": "present simple: affirmative with have",
      "title_form": "Presente simple: afirmativo con have",
      "title_target": "Present simple: affirmative with have",
      "description_md_form": "El verbo **have** (tener) se usa para hablar de posesiones, habilidades y experiencia. En presente simple afirmativo, la forma cambia según el sujeto:\n\n- **I / you / we / they** → **have**\n- **He / she / it** → **has**\n\nEjemplos:\n- `I have experience in sales.`\n- `She has good skills with people.`\n\n**Importante:** En inglés, **have** ya incluye la idea de posesión. No necesitas agregar otra palabra como *tengo*.\n\nPara hablar de experiencia en un área, usa el chunk: `I have experience in + área`.\n\n**Recuerda:** Con **he / she / it**, la forma es **has**, no *have*. Este es el error más común para hispanohablantes.",
      "description_md_target": "The verb **have** is used to talk about possessions, skills, and experience. In the present simple affirmative, the form changes with the subject:\n\n- **I / you / we / they** → **have**\n- **He / she / it** → **has**\n\nExamples:\n- `I have experience in sales.`\n- `She has good skills with people.`\n\n**Important:** In English, **have** already includes the idea of possession. You don't need to add another word like *tengo*.\n\nTo talk about experience in an area, use the chunk: `I have experience in + area`.\n\n**Remember:** With **he / she / it**, the form is **has**, not *have*. This is the most common mistake for Spanish speakers.",
      "grammar_structure": "Subject + have/has + (experience in + noun) / (noun)",
      "conjugation_table": {
        "name": "present_simple_have",
        "headers": [
          "Pronombre",
          "Forma",
          "Ejemplo"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "I",
            "have",
            "I have skills."
          ],
          [
            "You",
            "have",
            "You have experience."
          ],
          [
            "He / She / It",
            "has",
            "She has qualifications."
          ],
          [
            "We",
            "have",
            "We have a team."
          ],
          [
            "They",
            "have",
            "They have success."
          ]
        ]
      },
